<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  ГЛАВНАЯ. The screen the app opens on.
  ============================================================================

  READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING THE SHAPE OF THIS FILE.

  `docs/design2026/13-start-screen.md` carries an OWNER OVERRULE dated 2026-07-26:
  its SCOPE is void and only its VISUAL language survives. A wave built this screen
  "from nothing" out of that document, replaced the inline server list and the
  subscription card with two navigation rows, and replaced the connect object -
  concentric rings, the running animation, the country flag - with a bare disc. The
  owner compared the two builds and rejected it:

      «как выглядела главная по функционалу такая и должна остаться»
      «и дизайн кнопки другой совсем, хотя был другой раньше и анимация была»
      «все должно быть вернуто с пилюлей и инфой о подписке под кнопкой»

  So: **Главная is a RESTYLE.** Same controls, same capabilities, same information,
  same motion, drawn on the component layer with tokens and the type ramp.

  WHAT IS ON THIS SCREEN, top to bottom:

      [ 56 ] the strip: отдача · время сессии · приём, and the add action
      [ 56 ] the account row                          layout_home_account.xml
      [  1 ] hairline, alpha 0 until the content scrolls
      [ 48 ] the status strip, only when a condition applies
      [ 24 ]
      [224 ] the connect object: three concentric rings, one disc, one glyph
      [ 16 ]
      [>=42] the status word, then the flag and the server it runs through
      [ 24 ]
      [  * ] the subscription card, one page per subscription
      [  * ] the server list, inline - this is the ONLY place a server is picked
      [ 24 ]

  or, when there is not one server to connect to, the gate block in place of the
  card and the list (layout_home_empty.xml). Never both.

  THE RINGS ARE BACK AND THEY ARE NOT DECORATION. `CLAUDE.md`'s ban on decorative
  gradients and glows is about PAGE BACKGROUNDS: no radial wash behind the whole
  screen, no accent halo bleeding out of the shield. The connect object's own three
  concentric rings are its state channel - one hue at three opacities, a geometry
  that never changes size - and they are the reason the owner recognised the screen.
  They come back. The page gradient and the halo glow do not.

  ZERO RAW VALUES. No dp, no sp, no hex, no fontFamily, no textSize anywhere in
  this file - every number is a token and every text element carries only a
  textAppearance.

  clipChildren / clipToPadding are false the whole way down because the confirm
  ring scales past its own frame.
-->
<androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/home_tab_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="?android:attr/colorBackground"
    android:clipChildren="false"
    android:clipToPadding="false"
    android:fillViewport="true"
    android:scrollbars="none">

    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/home_content"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:clipChildren="false"
        android:orientation="vertical"
        android:paddingBottom="@dimen/space_24">

        <!--
          THE STRIP AND THE ADD ACTION, on one line, at the top - where this screen
          has always carried them, and in the order it always carried them:
          отдача, время сессии, приём.

          THE UNIT LIVES IN THE LABEL so the value stays a pure figure and the
          tabular advance has nothing else on the line to fight.

          THE RESERVE IS THE WHOLE POINT: android:minEms reserves N em, and an em IS
          the text size, so the reserve scales with the type at every font scale
          without a single sp literal. A value going 9,9 -> 10,1 moves nothing, and
          neither does 00:09:59 -> 00:10:00.

          The strip is on screen at rest, reading zeroes, exactly as it was: this is
          the screen's ledger, not a reward for connecting, and a row that vanishes
          when idle is a row the user cannot find. HomeFragment lands the figures on
          it while a tunnel is up and returns them to zero when it goes.
        -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/home_top_row"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:baselineAligned="false"
            android:gravity="center_vertical"
            android:orientation="horizontal"
            android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
            android:paddingEnd="@dimen/space_4">

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/numeric_strip"
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:baselineAligned="false"
                android:orientation="horizontal">

                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:orientation="vertical">

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/tv_up"
                        style="@style/TextAppearance.App.Numeric"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:minEms="3"
                        android:text="@string/home_speed_zero"
                        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Title"
                        tools:text="3,1" />

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/tv_up_label"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_4"
                        android:ellipsize="end"
                        android:maxLines="1"
                        android:text="@string/home_strip_up_label"
                        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption" />
                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- The session clock. Its own column, because "how long have I been
                     protected" is a different question from "how fast is it". -->
                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:orientation="vertical">

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/tv_uptime"
                        style="@style/TextAppearance.App.Numeric"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:minEms="5"
                        android:text="@string/home_uptime_zero"
                        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Title"
                        tools:text="00:12:04" />

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/tv_uptime_label"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_4"
                        android:ellipsize="end"
                        android:maxLines="1"
                        android:text="@string/home_strip_uptime_label"
                        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption" />
                </LinearLayout>

                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:orientation="vertical">

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/tv_down"
                        style="@style/TextAppearance.App.Numeric"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:minEms="3"
                        android:text="@string/home_speed_zero"
                        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Title"
                        tools:text="24,8" />

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/tv_down_label"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_4"
                        android:ellipsize="end"
                        android:maxLines="1"
                        android:text="@string/home_strip_down_label"
                        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption" />
                </LinearLayout>
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- The add action, top right, where it has always been. Adding a
                 subscription is the one thing this screen owns that is not the
                 connection, so it sits apart from the ledger of figures and opens
                 the SAME menu every other add entry point does. 48dp box, 24dp
                 glyph: the touch-target floor with no fixed height on its row. -->
            <ImageView
                android:id="@+id/btn_home_add"
                android:layout_width="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
                android:layout_height="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackgroundBorderless"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:contentDescription="@string/home_add_subscription"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:padding="@dimen/space_12"
                android:scaleType="fitCenter"
                app:srcCompat="@drawable/ic_add_24dp"
                app:tint="?attr/colorOnSurface" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- Rows bleed to the screen edge so their press feedback does; each row
             carries the 16dp gutter itself, from @style/Widget.Departament.Row. -->
        <include
            android:id="@+id/layout_home_account"
            layout="@layout/layout_home_account" />

        <!-- The ONLY scroll-linked change on this screen: no colour step, no
             elevation, no shadow, no collapsing title. -->
        <View
            android:id="@+id/header_hairline"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/stroke_hairline"
            android:alpha="0"
            android:background="?attr/colorOutlineVariant"
            android:importantForAccessibility="no" />

        <!-- The shared status-strip component in its INLINE placement: a persistent
             CONDITION, no auto-dismiss. Its hairline is hidden and its bar is
             clipped to @dimen/radius_control from HomeFragment, which is the only
             difference from the shell's docked placement of the same file. -->
        <include
            android:id="@+id/layout_status_strip"
            layout="@layout/view_status_strip"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_12"
            android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter" />

        <Space
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/space_24" />

        <!--
          THE CONNECT OBJECT. THREE CONCENTRIC RINGS, ONE DISC, ONE GLYPH.

          The rings are the reason the owner recognised the screen, and the reason he
          did not recognise the build that dropped them. They are not decoration
          around the object - they ARE the object's state channel: one colour at
          three rising opacities, outermost faintest, so the whole assembly reads
          idle grey, negotiating amber-blue, connected accent, failed red, on a
          geometry that never changes size.

          THE WHOLE ASSEMBLY IS THE CONTROL. connect_frame is 176 + 24 either side =
          224dp of touch target and @anim/press_scale scales rings, disc and shield
          together, because they are one object. The ring colours, the ripple and the
          2dp focus ring are built in HomeFragment from theme attributes - a drawable
          file cannot carry a runtime-tinted stroke without the raw hex the old
          bg_connect_ring.xml shipped, and two of that file's six hex literals
          measured 2.33:1 and 1.29:1 against the ground.

          The banned parts of the old hero did NOT come back with the rings: there is
          no accent glow bleeding out behind the shield and no page gradient under
          the screen. The breathing that used to live on that glow lives on the rings
          now, where it is the object telling you it is negotiating.
        -->
        <FrameLayout
            android:id="@+id/connect_frame"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_gravity="center_horizontal"
            android:clickable="true"
            android:clipChildren="false"
            android:clipToPadding="false"
            android:focusable="true"
            android:padding="@dimen/space_24"
            android:stateListAnimator="@anim/press_scale"
            tools:ignore="ContentDescription">

            <!-- Rings 3 and 2 of 3 are two layers of THIS view's background, inset
                 12dp apart, because a child of a padded FrameLayout can never be
                 wider than the padded box and the outer rings have to be. Ring 1 is
                 the disc's own. All three are built in HomeFragment.

                 The disc. Its fill and its own ring - the innermost and brightest of
                 the three - are built there too. -->
            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/connect_disc"
                android:layout_width="@dimen/connect_disc"
                android:layout_height="@dimen/connect_disc"
                android:layout_gravity="center"
                android:clipChildren="false">

                <!-- The confirm ring. Emitted exactly ONCE, at the instant the
                     tunnel confirms, and by no other event in the product. Never
                     loops, and there is never a second ring. -->
                <View
                    android:id="@+id/connect_ring_pulse"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:visibility="invisible" />

                <!-- The negotiating sweep. indicatorSize == the disc, so the arc
                     travels the disc's own ring instead of orbiting outside it, at
                     that ring's stroke width; the static ring underneath IS the
                     track. It runs while the core is negotiating and while a
                     subscription is being fetched - the two states this screen has
                     ever spun it for. -->
                <com.google.android.material.progressindicator.CircularProgressIndicator
                    android:id="@+id/connect_sweep"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:indeterminate="true"
                    android:visibility="gone"
                    app:hideAnimationBehavior="inward"
                    app:indeterminateAnimationType="disjoint"
                    app:indicatorColor="?attr/colorPrimary"
                    app:indicatorSize="@dimen/connect_disc"
                    app:showAnimationBehavior="inward"
                    app:trackColor="@android:color/transparent"
                    app:trackCornerRadius="@dimen/stroke_emphasis"
                    app:trackThickness="@dimen/stroke_ring" />

                <!-- Two shields, crossfaded. Never tint-animated: the filled shield
                     is accent from frame zero and only its alpha moves. -->
                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/shield_outline"
                    android:layout_width="@dimen/shield_glyph"
                    android:layout_height="@dimen/shield_glyph"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    app:srcCompat="@drawable/ic_shield_outline"
                    app:tint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/shield_filled"
                    android:layout_width="@dimen/shield_glyph"
                    android:layout_height="@dimen/shield_glyph"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:alpha="0"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    app:srcCompat="@drawable/ic_shield_filled"
                    app:tint="?attr/colorPrimary" />
            </FrameLayout>
        </FrameLayout>

        <Space
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/space_16" />

        <!-- THE STATUS LINE. This and an empty state are the only centred text in
             the product. There is NO status dot: the word carries the state and its
             colour reinforces it, which is already two channels. The word is
             swapped instantly, never crossfaded - it is the one string that has to
             be legible in four seconds. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/status_line"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
            android:gravity="center_horizontal"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
            android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter">

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/tv_status"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:maxLines="1"
                android:text="@string/home_status_disconnected"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Title" />

            <!-- WHAT IT RUNS THROUGH: the country flag and the server identity,
                 under the object, which is the second of the three questions this
                 screen answers. The flag is a 28dp fitting resolved by FlagUtil, and
                 the name beside it never repeats it.

                 INVISIBLE, never GONE: the line is always reserved, so nothing below
                 it moves when the detail appears or goes. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/server_identity"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                android:baselineAligned="false"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:visibility="invisible"
                tools:visibility="visible">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/tv_server_flag"
                    android:layout_width="@dimen/flag_size"
                    android:layout_height="@dimen/flag_size"
                    android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_8"
                    android:background="@drawable/bg_flag_tile"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                    tools:text="🇳🇱" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/tv_status_detail"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                    tools:text="Нидерланды, Амстердам · 48 мс" />
            </LinearLayout>
        </LinearLayout>

        <Space
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/space_24" />

        <!--
          THE SUBSCRIPTION SLOT. The subscription card and the server list, or the
          gate block, never both. HomeFragment crossfades between them in place.
        -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/subscription_slot"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:orientation="vertical">

            <!--
              THE SUBSCRIPTION CARD - a swipeable carousel, one page per subscription,
              carrying that subscription's name, its traffic pill, its last update and
              auto-update interval, the operator's notice, and its own actions:
              refresh, ping, pin, support, Telegram, delete (long press), and the
              chevron that collapses the list below.

              It is a CARD on this screen and not a «Подписка» row that navigates
              away: the owner's screen shows the subscription here, and the actions
              act on the page you are looking at.

              ViewPager2 cannot wrap_content, so HomeFragment measures every page and
              fixes the height to the tallest - one stable height, so peeking
              neighbours stay aligned. Page dots appear only past one subscription.
            -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/group_home_meta"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="vertical">

                <androidx.viewpager2.widget.ViewPager2
                    android:id="@+id/vp_home_meta"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:clipToPadding="false"
                    android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                    android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter" />

                <LinearLayout
                    android:id="@+id/ll_home_meta_dots"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="center_horizontal"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                    android:gravity="center_vertical"
                    android:orientation="horizontal"
                    android:visibility="gone" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!--
              THE SERVER LIST, INLINE, right below the card that owns it.

              This is the ONLY place in the product a server can be picked: the
              owner removed the Серверы destination on 2026-07-26 and none of its
              functions were moved elsewhere, so a Главная without this list would
              leave the app with no server selection at all.

              Tapping a row SELECTS, and never connects; when a tunnel is up the
              shell offers an explicit «применить». That contract lives in
              MainActivity.setSelectServer and is not this screen's to change.

              nestedScrollingEnabled=false: it scrolls with the page, it does not
              scroll inside it. HomeFragment pads its bottom by the shell's
              listBottomInset so the last row clears the overlaid bottom bar.
            -->
            <androidx.recyclerview.widget.RecyclerView
                android:id="@+id/rv_home_servers"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                android:clipToPadding="false"
                android:nestedScrollingEnabled="false"
                android:scrollbars="none" />

            <!-- Offline: the card and the rows keep their last value and the screen
                 says so, rather than emptying. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/tv_stale_hint"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:text="@string/home_stale_hint"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:visibility="visible" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <include
            android:id="@+id/layout_gate"
            layout="@layout/layout_home_empty" />
    </LinearLayout>
</androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView>
